[?2004l[?2004hroot@c6fdf7027b00:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation: Intrusion Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> An external threat actor targeted host `struts-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname:1`) originating from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The attacker exploited an OGNL injection vulnerability (CVE-2023-50164) in Apache Struts2 (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`) to plant a JSP web shell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Following initial entry, the attacker executed commands via Unix shell, staged a database archive at `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:2`), exfiltrated sensitive data over HTTPS to `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`), established persistence via root SSH authorized_keys (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`) and a cron job in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`), and attempted defense evasion by selectively wiping system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target Host Name**: `struts-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname:1`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Source / Exfil IP**: `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Domain**: `update-struts.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Monero Pool Endpoint**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.struts.evil:3333` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. End-to-End Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Step | MITRE ATT&CK Technique | Description | SAS Feed Coverage | Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | **T1190**: Exploit Public-Facing Application | Apache Struts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164) exploited via web request | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | **T1505.003**: Web Shell | JSP web shell dropped at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | **T1059.004**: Unix Shell | Interactive command execution via web shell interface | **SILENT** | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | **T1560.001**: Archive via Utility | Staging database dump archive at `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | **T1048**: Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol | Exfiltration of staged archive over HTTPS POST to `198.51.100.167` | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | **T1098.004**: SSH Authorized Keys | Planted backdoor public key in `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | **SILENT** | `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | **T1053.003**: Cron | Persistence via cron entry in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` invoking C2 payload | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | **T1070.002**: Clear System Logs | Selective wiping of system authentication logs | **SILENT** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Disambiguation of Benign System Activities
[?2004l[?2004h> During the investigation, an archive at `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) was analyzed.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Contains `# scheduled maintenance (BENIGN â€” legitimate ops job)` running `0 3 * * * root /usr/local/bin/backup.sh --remote 10.10.246`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Conclusion**: Confirmed as an approved, legitimate system administration job (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:2`, `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`). It is **not** part of the malicious campaign.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@c6fdf7027b00:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Vulnerability Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Common Weakness Enumeration**: CWE-552 (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties / Path Traversal)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVSS Score**: 9.8 (Critical) v3.1
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Affected Component**: Apache Struts2 Core (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deployment Location**: Mounted on Apache Tomcat server (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Exploitation Mechanics & Initial Access Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> An attacker at external IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`) manipulated file upload parameters to execute path traversal and bypass upload restrictions. This enabled the arbitrary write of a malicious JSP file into the web server directory structure.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Initial Upload Payload**: Attacker issued `POST /uploads/shell.php` / file upload payload (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Web Shell Placement**: The file traversal succeeded, creating an executable JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Execution Verification**: The attacker accessed the deployed JSP web shell to execute shell commands (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Disconfirming Unrelated / Stale Vulnerabilities
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: Listed in draft ticket CHG-7100 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Reconciliation Finding**: BlueKeep is a Microsoft Remote Desktop Services (RDP) vulnerability affecting Windows. Host `struts-prod-01` is a RHEL Linux machine (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`, `/disk/etc/hostname:1`) running Apache Tomcat. BlueKeep is **not** applicable to this host.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@c6fdf7027b00:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline and Configuration Weaknesses Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Vulnerable Software Baseline (BAS-01)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Presence of vulnerable library `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness**: Software dependency baseline was not updated to a patched Struts2 release, leaving host vulnerable to CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Allows unauthenticated Remote Code Execution (RCE) via web file upload requests.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. SSH Access Control & Key Management Baseline
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Unauthorized SSH public key added to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness**: Absence of file integrity monitoring (FIM) or baseline drift detection on `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Persistent administrative backdoor access bypassing password and multi-factor controls.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Web Application Executable Permissions & Storage Baseline
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Execution of dynamic JSP scripts permitted inside static assets directory `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness**: Insufficient web server access controls and lack of execution suppression in static asset directories.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Allows uploaded web shells to execute arbitrary system code.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Scheduled Task Monitoring Baseline
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Malicious beacon scheduled in `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness**: Lack of automated auditing and integrity monitoring over `/var/spool/cron/` entries.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Automated recurring command execution for persistent C2 connectivity and payload re-infection.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 5. Audit Logging & Anti-Forensic Resilience Baseline
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Selective wiping of Linux system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness**: Absence of centralized, immutable remote log forwarding (SIEM / Syslog-ng / Fluentd).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Attacker can alter or destroy local log evidence to evade detection and hinder forensic analysis.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
