# Investigation Progress & Working Checklist

## Investigation Timeline
- **2026-08-08 03:11:42 UTC**: Attacker at `198.51.100.167` initiates malicious file upload attempt (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).
- **2026-08-08 03:12:05 UTC**: Attacker attempts JNDI/LDAP lookup via parameter manipulation (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:392`).

==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==
# Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation: Intrusion Report

## 1. Executive Summary
An external threat actor targeted host `struts-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname:1`) originating from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The attacker exploited an OGNL injection vulnerability (CVE-2023-50164) in Apache Struts2 (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`) to plant a JSP web shell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`).


==> /app/vuln-report.md <==
# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report

## 1. Vulnerability Overview
- **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`)
- **Common Weakness Enumeration**: CWE-552 (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties / Path Traversal)

==> /app/baseline-report.md <==
# Baseline and Configuration Weaknesses Report

## 1. Vulnerable Software Baseline (BAS-01)
- **Finding**: Presence of vulnerable library `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).
